t  theory went that 13 year old diego  castillo the son of anton and a major  character throughout the story would  actually grow up to become vas that  would allow far cry 6 to link to vasa's  life without dealing with the one big  issue about bringing the character back  voss died in far cry 3. the post-credits  scene makes it definitively clear that  voss and diego are not the same person  still we're left with a lot of questions  about how the two games are linked and  what the return of vos might mean so  let's talk about what's actually in the  post-credits scene from the sounds of  things juan is meeting vos for a  business deal juan says that deposing  castillo has tripled the production of  viviro the life-saving cancer drug yara  creates in the game vos seems to be his  black market contact juan is selling  viviro and voss is buying it since he's  a drug smuggler and a pirate in far cry  3 that all tracks what's not clear is  whether this scene and far cry 6 in  general take place before or after far  cry 3. if it's before then voss might  just be a smuggler selling viviro  sometime before he's killed in far cry 3  making far cry 6 a bit of a prequel but  if it's after that tells us that vos  must have survived his apparent demise  in fc3 that seems fully possible since  your battle with vos in that game was  already a strange dreamlike vision we  don't really get enough information in  far cry 6 to know for sure when that  story takes place so we can't be sure if  vos survived far cry 3 or not but if vas  is still alive this scene makes some  suggestions for the future of yara it  calls into question juan's motives as a  member of the libertad freedom fighters  which is something the game has already  done a couple of times along the way it  raises some possibilities about the idea  of dany's ally becoming a potential  enemy sometime in the future as multiple  forces vie for control of the country  and the lucrative vivero production  industry it also suggests that vas  remains something of a powerful criminal  and pirate possibly working for himself  now rather than serving a higher boss as  in far cry 3. we don't know much about  juan and vaz's relationship but their  shady dealings probably aren't good news  for a country that just overthrew a  dictator and is lacking a stable  government as for what's next for vos  and far cry it depends on whether the  character might be woven into far cry  6's story once you've finished the game  you can continue to play far cry 6  fighting castio's military holdouts new  targets spring up each week as you work  to root out the loyalists and along with  the aforementioned dlc expansion that  suggests we could see more of the story  of yara down the road since juan is  already interacting with vas he might be  part of that story and we could see him  turn up as a villain or in some other  capacity opposite dany in post-release  content then again the post-credits  scene could just be a tease for a new  far cry title and merely functions to  set up the fact that vos is alive out  there and smuggling drugs in any case  it's clear that there's more vos coming  to far cry in the future in some form or  another  you
 

